.TH SMTDATA 1
.SH NAME
smtdata \- the dataset, from competition results and the features of their formulas
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B smtdata
[
.B \-s
.I solver
]
[
.B \-l
.I logic
]...
[
.B \-f
.I feats.tsv
]...
[
.I results.json.gz
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I smtdata
reads the results of one edition of SMT-COMP, from the file named or from the standard
input, in the
.I json
the competition publishes, gzipped or not, and writes the dataset: one line a
benchmark, with what a solver did of it and what the benchmark looks like.
.PP
A result is kept when it is of
.I solver
.RB ( \-s )
and of one of the
.I logics
.RB ( \-l ,
as many as given), when the solver gave an answer, and when one of the tables of
features
.RB ( \-f ,
as many as given, and at least one)
holds the benchmark.
Of the rest nothing is written, and a line on the standard error counts each
kind left out.
.PP
The columns come as
.BR id ,\  logic ,\  family ,\  status ,\  result ,\  wall ,\  cpu ,
then the feature columns in the order of the tables.
The family is the first folder of the benchmark under its logic,
and the status is the answer the formula declares, or unknown.
A timeout and an out of memory both come out as the class
.BR timeout .
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
The dataset of one solver over two logics:
.RS
.nf
smtdata \-s cvc5 \-l QF_BV \-l QF_ABV \e
	\-f QF_BV.tsv \-f QF_ABV.tsv results-sq-2025.json.gz > dataset.tsv
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
The tables of features are as
.IR smtfeat (1)
writes them, and must agree on their columns.
.SH SOURCE
The results are those of the single query track, as processed data at
.BR https://github.com/SMT-COMP/smt-comp.github.io/tree/master/data .
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.IR smtfeat (1),
.IR smtstat (1),
.IR smtfit (1)
